Metrics Deep Dive

🔹 What are Metrics? 📊
 Metrics are numerical data points collected over time that help you understand system performance and behavior.
 They answer: 👉 “How is my system performing right now?”

🔹 Why it matters in real-world? 🏗️
 In production, you can’t manually check everything.
 Metrics give you real-time visibility into your system and help detect issues early 🚨

🔹 Types of Metrics: ⚡
✔ Counter 🔢
Only increases (never decreases)
Used for counting events
👉 Example: Number of requests handled
✔ Gauge 📉
Can increase or decrease
Represents current value
👉 Example: CPU usage, memory usage
✔ Histogram 📊
Measures distribution of values
Helps track performance over time
👉 Example: API response time

🔹 Real-world Examples: 💡
👉 Counter → Total API requests = 10,000
 👉 Gauge → CPU usage = 75%
 👉 Histogram → Response time varies (100ms–500ms)

🔹 Key Concepts to Remember: 🧠
✔ Metrics = Numbers over time 📊
 ✔ Counter = Only increases 🔢
 ✔ Gauge = Goes up/down 📉
 ✔ Histogram = Performance distribution 📊
